# # M.5 Derivation [DERIVATION]
#
# Template: bereshit/word/seed/data/dotfiles/gitmessage.gitmessage
# Parent: B-word-omni-seed-data.omni
# Standard: Building Block Method commit types

# # M.6 Classification [CLASSIFICATION]
#
# Tags: git, commit, template, version-control, infrastructure
# Category: Rails (version control infrastructure)
# Paradigm: CPI-SI framework component

# # M.7 Intent [INTENT]
#
# Purpose: Guide developers to write clear, searchable commit messages
#
# Features:
#   - Subject line with domain keying ([DOMAIN/path] TYPE: Description)
#   - Building Block Method types (INIT, BUILD, REFINE, etc.)
#   - Structured body sections (What, Why, Scope, Keys)
#   - Consistent format across all contributors

# # M.8 Grounding [GROUNDING]
#
# Anchor: "A word fitly spoken is like apples of gold in pictures of silver."
#         - Proverbs 25:11
#
# Principle: Commit messages tell the story of the codebase. Each commit is
# a chapter that future developers will read to understand why decisions
# were made. Write with grace and clarity.

# # M.9 Dependencies [DEPENDENCIES]
#
# What This Needs:
#   - Git: Version control system
#   - Git Config: commit.template set to this file
#
# What Uses This:
#   - git commit (opens editor with template pre-filled)
#   - commit-msg hook (validates format)
#
# Integration:
#   - Global: git config --global commit.template ~/.gitmessage
#   - Local: git config commit.template .gitmessage

# # M.10 Roadmap [ROADMAP]
#
# Current: Template for standardized commit messages
# Next: Integration with commit-msg validation hook
# Future: Automated changelog generation from commit history
#
